    <article class="ba-body">
      <p>Moringa oleifera is a fast-growing tree native to the foothills of the Himalayas in northern India. Its small, rounded leaves are dried and milled into a vivid green powder.</p><p>On our label you'll find a single ingredient — Moringa leaf — and nothing else.</p>
      <h2 id="highlights">Highlights</h2><ul class="ba-hl"><li>Botanical name: Moringa oleifera.</li><li>Part used: leaf.</li><li>Taste: fresh, grassy, slightly earthy.</li><li>A natural source of vitamins and minerals such as calcium and iron (see the Nutrition Facts panel).</li></ul>
      <h2 id="s0">From tree to powder</h2><p>Leaves are harvested, gently dried to protect their colour, then milled in small batches. Bright green colour is a good sign of careful drying.</p><h2 id="s1">What a serving contains</h2><p>According to our label, one serving (2 rounded teaspoons, about 6 g) contains around 10 calories, with calcium and iron listed on the Nutrition Facts panel.</p><h2 id="s2">How people use it</h2><p>Moringa pairs best with fruit: smoothies, juices and green lattes. Start with half a teaspoon if you're new to its taste.</p>
